Short answer
- In most situations yes — use the same spelling that appears in the Social Security Administration (SSA) records (the name on your Social Security card). Many employers, banks, and government systems match your name to the SSA/IRS record and a mismatch can cause delays or rejections.

Why it matters
- Agencies that verify identity against SSA/IRS databases expect the name to match their records. If the name on the form differs (different spelling, missing/extra middle name or initial, wrong suffix), the check can fail.
